# The Android half of the telemetry configuration (spec §18.7).
#
#     cp android/telemetry.properties.example android/telemetry.properties
#
# `android/telemetry.properties` is untracked; the same two names in the environment work just as
# well. Copied as it stands, with both values empty, **the client is inert**: nothing is queued and
# nothing is sent (conventions.md, Configuration — no endpoint is ever defaulted in code). Gradle
# compiles whatever is here into BuildConfig; an empty value becomes a real `null`.
#
# No escaping problem here, unlike the iOS xcconfig: a properties file takes the URL as it is.

# The collector (spec §18.6): https://ingest.nann.in/smash
SMASH_TELEMETRY_URL=

# On the box: `grep SH_INGEST_TOKEN /opt/smashhockey/.env`. Not a secret in any real sense — it ships
# inside the APK — but it never belongs in a commit, a ticket or a chat.
SMASH_TELEMETRY_TOKEN=
